# avg_structure.in — average structure over the equilibrated window (step 1 of 2)
#
# RMSF measures fluctuation around each atom's mean position, so the reference
# must be the average structure of the trajectory itself. Computing that average
# requires the frames to be aligned first, which is why this is a two-step
# procedure: align to an arbitrary frame here, then realign to the average in
# rmsf.in.
#
# Usage: cpptraj -i avg_structure.in > avg_structure.log 2>&1
# Replace SYSTEM, REP and NRES before running.

parm SYSTEM_dry.prmtop

# Preliminary alignment target
reference SYSTEM_prod_REP_dry.nc 1

# Equilibrated window only — the initial drift is systematic, not fluctuation.
# 100 frames = 1 ns here (5,000 frames over 50 ns); 2501-5000 = last 25 ns.
trajin SYSTEM_prod_REP_dry.nc 2501 5000

# Remove global translation and rotation before averaging
rms fit_first reference :1-NRES@CA

# Average structure; written for all atoms, since it serves as a reference
# structure. The restriction to Ca happens in the masks, not here.
average avg_REP.rst7

go
